<DocsLayout title="Telemetry" description="Configure local tracing and optional OpenTelemetry OTLP export for Hologram Live.">
  <h1>Telemetry</h1>
  <p>Hologram Live uses <code>tracing</code> for structured local diagnostics and OpenTelemetry for optional OTLP/gRPC trace and metric export.</p>

  <h2>Enable OTLP export</h2>
  <pre><code>[telemetry]
enabled = true
endpoint = "http://127.0.0.1:4317"
service_name = "hologram-live"
export_timeout_secs = 5</code></pre>
  <p>The collector endpoint can also be set with <code>OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT</code>. Loopback HTTP is accepted for local collectors; remote collectors must use HTTPS.</p>

  <h2>What is recorded</h2>
  <div class="doc-grid">
    <article class="doc-card"><h3>Traces</h3><p>gRPC call spans include service, method, operation, and principal identity fields.</p></article>
    <article class="doc-card"><h3>Metrics</h3><p>RPC request counts and duration histograms are labeled by operation and outcome.</p></article>
  </div>

  <h2>Change local verbosity</h2>
  <pre><code>hologram tracing get
hologram tracing set 'info,hologram_live=trace'</code></pre>
  <p>Changing the tracing filter does not change audit behavior. Audit events use a separate bounded actor and durable file boundary.</p>

  <div class="note"><strong>Privacy boundary</strong>Do not add authorization headers, tokens, raw prompts, response bodies, private keys, or uploaded bytes to span fields.</div>
</DocsLayout>
